<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-4a ICallerContext and Dataverse client</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Task tags include auth and bff-api; modifies .cs files (DataverseUserClient, CallerWhoAmIMemo, the request pipeline)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security/auth-sensitive (tag auth): the caller identity behind every OBO call; new abstraction consumed across the decision slice</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, authorization, di, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add a scoped ICallerContext that wraps Spaarke.Core.Auth.CallerIdentity plus Principal, BearerToken and CorrelationId, populate it once per request, and make DataverseUserClient and CallerWhoAmIMemo read it instead of IHttpContextAccessor, so the decision slice (012) and MCP tools run as the caller without HttpContext.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core authentication, OBO token flows and scoped dependency injection.</role>
  <goal>ICallerContext and its scoped implementation exist; one middleware fills it once per request right after app.UseAuthorization(); DataverseUserClient and CallerWhoAmIMemo read it; an unpopulated context fails closed with DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED; T170's one-WhoAmI-per-commit count is unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-10, design §8 B-4. CallerResolution.cs:63-66 already forbids HttpContext overloads. B-4 is split in two (notes/decisions.md 2026-11-06): this task is the context and the Dataverse client; 012 threads it through the decision services. unified-access-control-r2 reviews this diff (project CLAUDE.md §4).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/ICallerContext.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/CallerContext.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/CallerContextMiddleware.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/MiddlewarePipelineExtensions.cs (register the middleware immediately after app.UseAuthorization(), L162)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SpaarkeCore.cs (registers DataverseUserClient; add AddScoped ICallerContext there)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs (IHttpContextAccessor at L49/L72; UserContextRequired at L172/L183)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/CallerWhoAmIMemo.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/CallerResolution.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/CallerIdentity.cs:106</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/DecisionCommitServiceTests.CallerIdentityCount.cs (T170 WhoAmI count)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/Signals/CallerWhoAmIMemoIsolationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Signals/CallerContextTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Auth/CallerContextTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisite task; startable in Wave 1.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">ICallerContext carries the existing Spaarke.Core.Auth.CallerIdentity and does not duplicate its fields or add a third caller type (naming note §1); the BearerToken it holds is used only for OBO inside the BFF and is never logged, returned in a response, or passed to any client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every operation this task adds or changes reads the caller only from ICallerContext (task 010); an unpopulated context returns DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED) and never falls back to an app-only client (FR-10, ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">ICallerContext is registered once as Scoped in Infrastructure/DI/SpaarkeCore.cs beside DataverseUserClient; no new DI module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">This task changes no authorization policy, authentication scheme or AuthorizationModule.cs code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope is DataverseUserClient, CallerWhoAmIMemo and the middleware only; the other IHttpContextAccessor uses (85 in 46 files) are out of scope, and the decision services are task 012.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">T170's per-commit WhoAmI count (DecisionCommitServiceTests.CallerIdentityCount.cs, WhoAmIs == 1) stays 1; the PR is reviewed by unified-access-control-r2 and gets two adversarial-reviewer passes (root CLAUDE.md §8.5, auth tag).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Every log statement or telemetry property this task adds records identifiers, sizes, timings and outcome/reason codes only: no bearer token, claim value, record text or tool argument (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any defect found and not fixed in this task is filed with /project-defer-issue-tracking (notes/defer-issues.md AND a GitHub issue), never one without the other (project CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
  </constraints>

