  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read CallerResolution.cs, CallerIdentity.cs, DataverseUserClient.cs, CallerWhoAmIMemo.cs and how the memo keys its per-request value today.</step>
    <step order="2">Define ICallerContext (read-only to consumers: CallerIdentity? Caller, ClaimsPrincipal? Principal, string? BearerToken, string CorrelationId, bool IsPopulated) and a scoped CallerContext with an internal populate method.</step>
    <step order="3">Add CallerContextMiddleware after app.UseAuthorization() that populates the context once per request from the authenticated principal, the Authorization bearer value and the existing correlation id.</step>
    <step order="4">Change DataverseUserClient and CallerWhoAmIMemo to read ICallerContext; an unpopulated context returns UserContextRequired without a Dataverse call.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the tests named in the acceptance criteria; run the Signals, auth and contract suites and the T170 test; record the WhoAmI count before and after in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Measure the publish-size delta; request unified-access-control-r2 review and run two adversarial-reviewer passes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If moving CallerWhoAmIMemo off HttpContext changes T170's WhoAmI count, STOP and escalate rather than adjusting the test (FAILURE-MODES AP-9).</trigger>
    <trigger>If populating the context needs an authentication-scheme or AuthorizationModule.cs change, STOP: that is an auth diff outside this task (root CLAUDE.md §6).</trigger>
    <trigger>If a DataverseUserClient consumer runs outside a request scope (e.g. a job continuation) and would now fail, STOP and list the path rather than adding an app-only fallback.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>CallerResolution.cs (resolves the caller; L63-66 forbids HttpContext overloads), CallerWhoAmIMemo.cs, IHttpContextAccessor in DataverseUserClient.cs:49/72, Spaarke.Core.Auth.CallerIdentity (CallerIdentity.cs:106).</existing>
    <extension>Partly: it wraps the existing CallerIdentity instead of adding a caller type, but a scoped holder is still needed because DataverseUserClient can reach the caller today only through IHttpContextAccessor.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>MCP tools and the decision capability can get the caller only by running inside an HTTP request; a non-HTTP continuation fails silently with UserContextRequired, and FR-10 ('no HttpContext in decision-slice methods') cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

