    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/CallerContextMiddleware.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Signals/CallerContextTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Auth/CallerContextTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an authenticated workforce request, ICallerContext is populated exactly once (Caller, Principal, BearerToken, CorrelationId) before the endpoint runs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DataverseUserClient.cs and CallerWhoAmIMemo.cs contain no IHttpContextAccessor or HttpContext reference (grep evidence in the PR).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a DataverseUserClient call in a scope whose ICallerContext is unpopulated returns DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED, makes no Dataverse call and uses no app-only client.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an anonymous request leaves ICallerContext unpopulated and the existing 401 behaviour is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T170_OneCommit_AsksWhoAmIOnce_AndAsksEveryRightsQuestion passes with WhoAmIs == 1, and CallerWhoAmIMemoIsolationTests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A log-capture test proves no added log line contains the bearer token or a claim value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing Signal, Decision, Caller and Dataverse tests in Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests and Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE), unified-access-control-r2's review and two adversarial-reviewer passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-10; design §8 B-4. A seeding proof is requested for the fail-closed test (fail-open would be a security outcome): make the unpopulated path fall through, confirm the test fails, restore. Run dotnet test without --no-build after edits (G-12).</notes>

